+## T11 — Inline-asset reconciliation replacing detection
+
+**Files changed:** `src/lib/agent/inlineAssets.ts`, `tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts`
+
+### Design
+
+Added `reconcileInlineAssets(sentTokens: string[], replyHtml: string): ReconcileResult`, pure, no I/O, next to the existing `extractInlineAssets`/`restoreInlineAssets`/`missingTokens` in the same file (kept unchanged, per ruling — caller wiring is T17).
+
+```ts
+export type ReconcileResult =
+  { kind: 'clean' } | { kind: 'restored'; missing: string[] } | { kind: 'mismatch'; reason: string }
+```
+
+Algorithm:
+
+1. Scan `replyHtml` for all token-shaped occurrences via a new module-level `TOKEN_RE`, built from the same `TOKEN_PREFIX`/`TOKEN_SUFFIX` constants `extractInlineAssets` already uses (one token pattern for the whole file — no second literal pattern defined) — ``new RegExp(`${TOKEN_PREFIX}.*?${TOKEN_SUFFIX}`, 'g')``, counting occurrences per exact token string (multiset).
+2. Any found token not in `sentTokens` → `mismatch` (covers renamed and reindexed placeholders).
+3. Any sent token found more than once → `mismatch` (covers duplicated placeholders).
+4. Otherwise, sent tokens absent from the reply are computed; none absent → `clean`; some absent → `restored` with the list.
+
+**One deliberate design decision worth flagging:** the token regex's middle is a _lazy wildcard_ (`.*?`), not `\d+`. A first draft used `\d+` (mirroring how tokens are minted: `TOKEN_PREFIX + index + TOKEN_SUFFIX`), but that made a genuinely-renamed token (e.g. `__INLINE_ASSET_RENAMED__`, prefix/suffix kept, index replaced with non-numeric content) invisible to the scanner — it would just look like the original token vanished, i.e. a clean absence (`restored`), not a mismatch. The controller ruling's own wording — "anything else (unknown token such as a reindexed `__INLINE_ASSET_7__` not sent, a sent token appearing twice, renamed tokens)" — groups "renamed" together with "unknown token", implying a renamed token must still be _recognized_ as a token-shaped string in order to be flagged as unknown. Switching to a lazy wildcard between the fixed prefix/suffix makes that true without changing any minted-token round-trip behavior (numeric indices still match the same way, just via `.*?` instead of `\d+`).
+
+### TDD evidence
+
+**RED** — added 7 new test cases to `tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts` (import updated to include `reconcileInlineAssets`) before writing the implementation:
+
+```
+$ npx vitest run tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts
+ FAIL  tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts > reconcileInlineAssets > reconciles clean when nothing was sent and nothing comes back
+TypeError: reconcileInlineAssets is not a function
+ FAIL  tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts > reconcileInlineAssets > restores a cleanly absent token (AC-06)
+TypeError: reconcileInlineAssets is not a function
+ FAIL  tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts > reconcileInlineAssets > treats a renamed token as a mismatch (AC-07)
+TypeError: reconcileInlineAssets is not a function
+ FAIL  tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts > reconcileInlineAssets > treats a duplicated token as a mismatch (AC-07)
+TypeError: reconcileInlineAssets is not a function
+ FAIL  tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts > reconcileInlineAssets > treats a reindexed token as a mismatch (AC-07)
+TypeError: reconcileInlineAssets is not a function
+ FAIL  tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts > reconcileInlineAssets > counts a token found inside an unrelated attribute, not only in src/url() position
+TypeError: reconcileInlineAssets is not a function
+ Test Files  1 failed (1)
+      Tests  7 failed | 7 passed (14)
+```
+
+(The one 7th "clean when the reply returns the same tokens (AC-05)" case also failed the same way — 7 new failures total, 7 pre-existing tests still green.)
+
+**GREEN (first pass, one residual failure)** — implemented with `\d+` middle:
+
+```
+$ npx vitest run tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts
+ FAIL  tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts > reconcileInlineAssets > treats a renamed token as a mismatch (AC-07)
+AssertionError: expected 'restored' to be 'mismatch'
+ Tests  1 failed | 13 passed (14)
+```
+
+This confirmed the `\d+`-vs-`.*?` reasoning above rather than a code bug — the "renamed" case needs the token wrapper recognized as unknown, not silently dropped. Switched `TOKEN_RE`'s middle from `\d+` to `.*?`.
+
+**GREEN (final)**:
+
+```
+$ npx vitest run tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts
+ Test Files  1 passed (1)
+      Tests  14 passed (14)
+```
+
+### Test cases (7 new, covering the brief's exact list)
+
+- AC-05: same N tokens back → `clean`
+- zero tokens sent & zero back → `clean`
+- AC-06: one placeholder cleanly absent → `restored`, `missing: [token]`
+- AC-07 renamed (`__INLINE_ASSET_RENAMED__` in place of a sent token) → `mismatch`
+- AC-07 duplicated (a sent token appears twice) → `mismatch`
+- AC-07 reindexed (`__INLINE_ASSET_99__`, never sent, in place of a sent token) → `mismatch`
+- a token-like string inside an unrelated attribute (`alt=""` alongside `src=""`) is still counted by the regex — in this test the token appears twice (src + alt) so it resolves to `mismatch` (duplicated), demonstrating the regex counts context-free occurrences rather than only `src=""`/`url()` positions
+
+### Files changed
+
+- `src/lib/agent/inlineAssets.ts` — added `TOKEN_RE`, `ReconcileResult`, `reconcileInlineAssets`. `extractInlineAssets`, `restoreInlineAssets`, `missingTokens` untouched (no caller rewiring — that's T17).
+- `tests/unit/inlineAssets.test.ts` — added `reconcileInlineAssets` to the import, added a new `describe('reconcileInlineAssets', ...)` block with the 7 cases above.
+- `tests/unit/prompts.test.ts` — added `SCRIPT_SUPPORT_NOTE`/`PROMPT_VERSION` to the import, added the T10 test block.
